From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: check firmware table indexes in the message
 handlers

Several message handlers index vif_table[] and sta_table[] (36 entries
each) with a u8 from the message and use the entry unchecked:
ps_change_ind, traffic_req_ind, rssi_status_ind, pktloss_notify_ind,
tkip_mic_failure_ind, tx_credits_update_ind, sm_connect_ind,
sm_disconnect_ind, sm_external_auth_required_ind and the mesh handlers.

Add rwnx_msg_vif() and rwnx_msg_sta(): they check the index, count a miss
in rx_bad_frame_drops and return NULL, and the handlers drop the message.
Also in these handlers: sm_disconnect_ind reads drv_conn_state before its
NULL check; mesh_peer_update_ind and tkip_mic_failure_ind and
sm_external_auth_required_ind use a NULL vif; sm_connect_ind indexes
chnl2bw[] (5 entries) with ind->width and sta_flowctrl[]
(NX_REMOTE_STA_MAX) with the AP entry; mesh_path_update_ind stores
sta_table[nhop_sta_idx] unchecked. These are checked as well.

Assisted-by: Claude

